// day and ~300 globally, on free-tier keys. Most visitors ask the same dozen
// things — what is this, how many tools, how does failover work, is it safe —
// and every one of those used to cost a real model call, so a visitor could
// burn their whole allowance on questions that were already answered in
// writing months ago.
//
// So: known questions are answered instantly from here, badged "from the
// docs", and the live agent stays one click away for anyone who wants to watch
// it actually run. The badge is not decoration — a page whose entire claim is
// "this one is real" cannot serve prose from a file under a "live" label.
//
// SOURCE OF TRUTH. Every answer below is drawn from two documents written
// about the real system:
//   · INTERVIEW_PITCH.html          — architecture, request trace, tools,
//                                     reliability, memory, honest gaps
//   · TOOL_CALLING_DEEP_DIVE.html   — schemas, tool routing, provider wire
//                                     formats, the Gemini signature quirk
// Nothing here is invented. Where the docs admit a gap, so does the answer —
// the "hard questions" section of the pitch is the most persuasive thing in
// either document and it would be absurd to launder it into marketing.

